AccountV3Policy / AccountV3Signatures
├── given a policy candidate
│   ├── when count, mode, roles, lengths, delays or thresholds are invalid -> reject
│   ├── when legacy mode or RECOVERY role is supplied -> deny
│   ├── when key is repeated through verifier/RP/kind aliases -> reject
│   ├── when membership is duplicated or unsorted -> reject
│   ├── when SPEND or ADMIN thresholds cannot be reached -> reject
│   └── when independent thresholds are reachable -> preserve the TS policy hash
├── given an explicitly typed signer
│   ├── ECDSA -> OZ recovery, low-S, exact digest; never automatic ERC-1271 dispatch
│   ├── WebAuthn -> actual pinned V3 verifier, exact TS wire bytes, bounded gas
│   └── ERC-1271 -> exact wallet/key/codehash and live revocable signature validation
│       ├── changed/revoked wallet authorization -> deny
│       ├── absent or changed verifier code -> deny
│       ├── revert, gas exhaustion, short/malformed/wrong magic -> deny
│       └── state-writing callback -> staticcall prevents mutation
└── given a quorum request
    ├── when role is unknown or combined -> deny
    ├── when too few/many, repeated or out-of-range members -> deny
    ├── when an extra signature is invalid -> deny the entire set
    ├── when signatures belong to another digest/role -> deny
    └── when distinct current members satisfy the selected threshold -> accept
        ├── user-owned consumer key can spend and administer without GatoPago
        └── no support/email/assisted authority exists
